HST Office: the File panel takes the window's width below the document tab strip.

The panel stopped left of the HASON TECH banner, as it did when it dropped from the tab row over the ribbon's
body, where the banner is. Since the panel starts below the document tab strip (owner, 14/11/2026), the banner
is above it, yet the panel still stopped at the banner's left edge: in a 1042 px window at 125 % on Windows that
left about 550 px, and the Print page lost its right part ("Quay lại", the printer's status, the preview). The
panel now stops at the banner only where the banner reaches below the panel's top (no document tab strip).

- sfx2/source/backstage/hstbackstageplacement.hxx (new, plain arithmetic, unit tested),
  sfx2/source/backstage/hstbackstagewindow.cxx (BackstageWindow::GetPlacement).

License: these upstream-derived files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_backstage_panel_placement.py; tests/runtime/check-backstage-print-fits.py (Windows, 125 %,
windows 1024-1366 px wide: the Print page's widgets lie inside the panel).

